 that somehow  we're deliberately trying to frustrate  the concept of equality at least in the  law everybody is assured here  you hear that we are not simon  as people we have one interest  and that is our collective and  individual rights and all i'm saying  here is that  as someone that represents both sides  i'd like to see the equality clause once  and for all  settled in the 1990s the canadian  government would ask simon  to serve as canada's ambassador for  circumpolar affairs  and canada's ambassador to denmark most  recently  she has worked to improve inuit  education mary simon has been a diplomat  she has been a leader she also has run  foundations  in relation to children and youth she's  been a tireless advocate  for inuit  simon says she fully expects to continue  her lifelong work advancing the  interests of  inuit and other indigenous peoples now  as the canadian representative  of queen elizabeth ii there are  very important responsibilities  associated with my role that will help  the working relationship of canadians  and indigenous people  and beginning monday she will begin that  new chapter  in a life of work for the arctic and its  peoples  david aiken global news ottawa and that  is global national for this sunday night  i'm jeff semple tonight's your canada is  this pair of blue jays in sydney nova  scotia  thanks for watching have a great night  [Music]  [Applause]  [Music]  you
 

